Build: add <cstdint> to nine pangolin headers/sources for GCC 15

GCC 15 stopped transitively including <cstdint>, so every pangolin translation unit
that names uint8_t/uint32_t without including it fails to compile. This is cause (1)
of the two that keep the pangolin 3D viewer from building; RUNBOOK.md records it as
solved, and this patch is what solves it.

Nine files need the include, not the eight an earlier note claimed --
include/pangolin/factory/factory_registry.h was missing from that list. Rather than
trust any list, drive it from the compiler's own diagnostic:

    note: 'uint32_t' is defined in header '<cstdint>'

That converges whether or not the list is right, which is why the count moved.

This does NOT make pangolin build. Cause (2) is unfixed: the conda toolchain compiles
against $CONDA_PREFIX/x86_64-conda-linux-gnu/sysroot and cannot see /usr/include, so
EGL/dc1394 headers installed with apt are invisible to it. See RUNBOOK.md "Parked: the
pangolin 3D viewer does not build" for why CPATH=/usr/include is the wrong bridge.

Unlike 0001 and 0002, this patch is NOT required to run SLAM -- the viewer is parked and
--headless avoids it entirely. It is here so the solved half of a parked problem is not
re-derived by hand from prose, since vendor/ is gitignored.

Upstream: luigifreda/pyslam master @ a5ff256 (no release tags exist).
Pangolin is vendored inside that tree at thirdparty/pangolin.

